## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/livevideo.html
- Summary (EN): The Live Video node captures images from a live video source such as a webcam or screen recorder and outputs them into a COP network. It runs as a non-deterministic live stream independent of the playbar and keyframes, which makes it useful as a sandbox.
- Résumé (FR) : Capture une source vidéo en direct (webcam, enregistrement d'écran) dans un réseau COP, de façon non déterministe et indépendante de la timeline.

- Key parameters: ["Source: video source to connect to; the options depend on the machine", "Configuration: format string (format, x resolution, y resolution, framerate) the source must support; set Source first", "Connect to Source: toggles the connection to the video source; this setting is not saved in the hip file", "Live Stream: when connected, enables interactive streaming independent of the playbar", "Toggle Live Stream: pauses and resumes the stream while Live Stream is on; the cooking controls button does the same", "Live Tick: shows the current tick within the live stream"]

- Caveats: ["The page documents no input connectors", "Sources and configurations are specific to the machine and may not work elsewhere", "Connect to Source must be re-enabled each time the hip file is opened", "Live Stream does not save results like other streaming types; use a Stash COP to store output", "Live Stream requires Connect to Source to be on", "The output is non-deterministic and not tied to keyframes or caching"]

